<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Girl from the North Country (Bob Dylan)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1963</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, borrowing lines from Carthy's arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Scarborough Fair/Canticle (Simon &amp; Garfunkel; arrangement in copyright)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1966</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (counterpoint with Simon's &quot;Canticle&quot;)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Version by Sérgio Mendes and Brasil '66</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1968</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as (used in the film Heavy Traffic, 1973)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Versions by Vicky Leandros in German, French and Greek</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1969</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Elizabeth My Dear (The Stone Roses)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1989</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Scarborough Fayre (Mediæval Bæbes)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2005</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Version by My Dying Bride with two added stanzas by Aaron Stainthorpe</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2009</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Version by Nox Arcana with new words by Joseph Vargo</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">English civilization theme in Civilization VI (Geoff Knorr)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Elfin Knight (Child 2)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1670</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the earlier ballad it shares its story with</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Riddles Wisely Expounded (Child 1)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">possible source of the refrain and the fair</span></li></ul></section>
